{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794890000000-engineer-d1-r26-closure-retention-expansion-replay.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r26 — addressed scratch snapshot-probe package\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. **Partial, below the items 1–3 checkpoint.** The r25 narrow probe's captured runtime, selected classpath archives and launch files now have a shared, addressed scratch package. A later process copied it, verified its manifest and every referenced object and file, and launched its package-local guarded test successfully. This is not yet the requested executable reconstruction closure, durable retention, a package-pinned expansion determination, or isolated retained-input replay. No D1 verification or historical runtime attestation is claimed. HEAD is detached at \"'`e4ac21142397d27bf6627121c29ddfb57a602970`; retained admissions, roots, outcomes and evidence remain unchanged.\n\n## Package and scratch-copy test\n\n`test/yang/correspondence_probe_package.py` creates a versioned, SHA-256-addressed package with an ordered role list, individual object sizes and hashes, and individual launch-file sizes and hashes. It verifies the source and copied bytes before publishing the package and independently verifies the addressed manifest, object identities, file identities and exact file sets. It refuses changed manifest addresses, altered or missing bytes, unexpected files, unsafe names and symlinked package directories. Its explicit scope is `observed-probe-inputs-not-reconstruction-closure`.\n\n`test/yang/correspondence_r26_probe_package.py` packages the r19 inventory'\"'s 151 selected ordered classpath objects and normalized runtime object, plus the r25 plan, snapshot and plan helpers, inventory and the package-local entrypoint. The package is \"'`target/d1-r26-probe-package` (427 MiB reported by `du`); it has **152 object roles / 152 distinct objects / 5 files**. The manifest address is SHA-256 `3becf11f14011eee349508fc18b32584ccd2f7589e1a5b7402ecc54035473dd9`; a worktree copy is `1794890000000-engineer-d1-r26-probe-package-manifest.json`. The inventory'\"'s recorded original host paths are descriptive, not paths used to load Java or its classpath.\n\nAfter the creation process exited, a separate launcher copied the package to a fresh scratch directory, verified the copy against the manifest address, and started a fresh isolated-mode host Python (\"'`-I -B`) to execute `correspondence_r26_package_entry.py` from the verified copy. That entrypoint extracted the verified package objects and invoked the package'\"'s restored Java and ordered classpath using the package's launch plan. The guarded static probe passed **1 test / 6 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors**. A further independent process reverified all 152 objects and five files in the retained scratch package. Commands, while these scratch artifacts are available:\n\n\"'```\nPYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=target/d1-r26-pycache python3 test/yang/correspondence_r26_probe_package.py verify target/d1-r26-probe-package 3becf11f14011eee349508fc18b32584ccd2f7589e1a5b7402ecc54035473dd9\nPYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=target/d1-r26-pycache python3 test/yang/correspondence_r26_probe_package.py launch target/d1-r26-probe-package 3becf11f14011eee349508fc18b32584ccd2f7589e1a5b7402ecc54035473dd9\n```\n\nThe outer verifier and Python interpreter are host/bootstrap inputs, not addressed in this package. Scratch-copy verification precedes entrypoint execution, but it is not a defense against concurrent modification by a hostile local process. This experiment still permits filesystem and network access and does not show that checkout, caches or other ambient paths were unavailable. The inner probe loads the macro namespace before arming two Vars, then runs the same fresh-admission producer-side test whose expected outputs are generated in the same process. It is not the ruling'\"'s retained-input-to-claimed-output replay, full expansion determination, or proof that all source/resource/native dependencies of a different entrypoint are present. In particular, r22's excluded generated directories and two Netty native entries are evidence only for the tested local path; the package retains the original Netty jars.\n\nThe manifest's SHA-256 identifies these bytes but does not designate an owner or ensure availability. \"'`target/` remains scratch; this is not the r7 durable location, an owner commitment, or the original producer'\"'s historical runtime. The r7 scratch-copy-before-open pattern was applied to this experimental package only.\n\n## Required continuation\n\nComplete and enforce the launch/build plan for the actual reconstruction entrypoint, including all result-affecting inputs and an explicit platform boundary. Derive and test its source/resource, binary and native dependency closure with checkout and caches unavailable; retain all required bytes in an identified durable location with a retention owner and retrieval mechanism. Then substantiate the expansion bypass against that pinned composition and checked execution path, or retain the applicable expansion context and events. Fetch and verify the complete package, run the retained-input adaptation, assembly and compilation/stamping from its compiler code, and compare all claimed outputs without manufacturing admission identities, roots or historical events. Independent correspondence, image/trace obligations and bounded publication remain separate.\n\n## Validation\n\n\"'`correspondence_probe_package_test.py` passed 2 tests after red-first cases for missing implementation, undeclared root files and a symlinked object directory being read before refusal. The tests also exercise changed manifest identity, changed object bytes, unsafe names and pre-existing destinations. The r25 launch-plan and archive-safety tests each passed 2 tests. clj-kondo on the manifest/dependency code and manifest/oracle tests reported 0 errors and 0 warnings; `git diff --check` passed. The frozen v1 `slice9_site_tables.edn` SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No full oracle suite, tagged lane, corpus reconstruction, publication or commit was run. The earlier two ruling filenames and continuation-4 remain unavailable under the supplied names, as documented in r17–r25; the third ruling and available findings were consulted.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
